message: "If you use or build on this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Delta Atlas / Resilience Ledger"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tiller
    given-names: Jake
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://resilience-eval-ai.pages.dev/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JakeTOpenSource/Resilience-Ledger"
date-released: 2026-09-24
abstract: >-
  The public record of one researcher's theory of agentic AI governance
  and the instruments built from it. BespokeNode, a state-delta
  governance framework (controlled path, HOLD versus TRIP, four
  invariants); Pin-Check, a skill that traces every precise value in a
  document to an artifact; OpenMirror, a method for turning a metaphor
  into policy one correspondence at a time, with the V=IR crosswalk as
  its worked example. Alongside: deterministic, client-side instruments
  (a function-first glossary of agentic AI governance, a framework
  audit, a gap check for plans, an ordering-drift detector for agent
  traces), the Resilience Ledger method documents and calibration logs.
  No model or external API is required at runtime; detector lexicons are
  versioned and openly displayed. Claims carry their status; nothing is
  called golden without the owner's explicit word.
keywords:
  - state-delta architecture
  - BespokeNode
  - agent governance
  - coherence audit
  - agentic AI governance
  - ordering drift
  - deterministic evaluation
  - plain-language glossary
  - resilience ledger
